{
 "id": "3-0-0",
 "title": "Disaster Types and India's Vulnerability",
 "emoji": "⚠️",
 "cards": [
  {
   "tag": "Why this matters",
   "h": "Nature gives hazards; people make disasters",
   "b": "<p>India sits on active plates, borders a warming ocean and has a monsoon climate. Millions of poor and unprepared people live in exposed places. UPSC treats disasters as <b>geography</b> (causes) and as <b>governance</b> (response). This lesson covers the first part.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Hazard, risk and vulnerability",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 130\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4dcd5\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"36\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Hazard</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"36\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">x</text><rect x=\"124\" y=\"10\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"169\" y=\"36\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Exposure</text><text x=\"226\" y=\"36\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">x</text><rect x=\"238\" y=\"10\" width=\"72\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"274\" y=\"36\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Vulnerability</text><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#5d6474\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"80\" width=\"180\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dceaec\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Capacity to cope</text></svg><p>A <b>hazard</b> is a dangerous event. A <b>disaster</b> happens when a hazard hits a vulnerable community. The <b>Disaster Management Act, 2005</b> defines a disaster as a catastrophe, mishap, calamity or grave occurrence that causes loss of life, property or damage to the environment beyond the community's capacity to cope.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Classification",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 182\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4dcd5\" stroke=\"#a3362a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"62.5\" y=\"29.0\" fill=\"#a3362a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Geological</text><rect x=\"121\" y=\"6\" width=\"189\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.5\" y=\"29.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Earthquake, volcano, tsunami, landslide</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dceaec\" stroke=\"#2f6f7a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"62.5\" y=\"73.0\" fill=\"#2f6f7a\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Hydro-meteorological</text><rect x=\"121\" y=\"50\" width=\"189\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.5\" y=\"73.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Flood, cyclone, drought, heat wave, cloudburst</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"94\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"62.5\" y=\"117.0\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Biological</text><rect x=\"121\" y=\"94\" width=\"189\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.5\" y=\"117.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Epidemic, pest attack, COVID-19</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"138\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"62.5\" y=\"161.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Man-made</text><rect x=\"121\" y=\"138\" width=\"189\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"215.5\" y=\"161.0\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Industrial leaks, fires, stampedes, CBRN</text></svg><p>Another split is by speed: <b>rapid onset</b> (earthquake, flash flood) and <b>slow onset</b> (drought, desertification). Disasters can cascade: a quake triggers a landslide, which blocks a river and floods a valley.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "India's vulnerability: the numbers",
   "b": "<svg class=\"d\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 188\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"6\" width=\"100\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Hazard</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"6\" width=\"200\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f1e4c6\" stroke=\"#a8792a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"210.0\" y=\"23\" fill=\"#7d5a1c\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">India's exposure (approx.)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"32\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Earthquake</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"32\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"210.0\" y=\"51\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 59% of area in zones III-V</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"62\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Flood</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"62\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"210.0\" y=\"81\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 40 m ha, 12% of land</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"92\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Cyclone</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"92\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"210.0\" y=\"111\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 5,700 km of coast</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Drought</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"122\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"210.0\" y=\"141\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 68% area prone</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"152\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">Landslide</text><rect x=\"110\" y=\"152\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f3f1ec\" stroke=\"#c9c2b6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"210.0\" y=\"171\" fill=\"#1d2433\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Himalaya, Ghats, NE</text></svg><p>These figures come from NDMA and similar sources; they change with updated maps. Most districts face at least one major hazard. Heat waves and lightning are now recognised as major killers.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Why India is so exposed",
   "b": "<p><b>Geography</b>: young Himalaya, a long coast, river basins in flood plains. <b>Climate</b>: monsoon variability, and warming seas. <b>Society</b>: dense population, poor housing, weak enforcement of building codes, encroachment on floodplains, and deforestation. Poverty is the biggest vulnerability, as poor people live in kutcha houses on risky land.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Major disasters to remember",
   "b": "<p><b>Bhopal gas leak</b> (1984), <b>Odisha super cyclone</b> (1999), <b>Bhuj quake</b> (2001), <b>Indian Ocean tsunami</b> (2004), <b>Mumbai floods</b> (2005), <b>Uttarakhand floods</b> (2013), <b>Chennai floods</b> (2015), <b>Kerala floods</b> (2018), <b>Chamoli</b> (2021), <b>Wayanad landslides</b> (July 2024, over 200 deaths), <b>Himachal and Sikkim</b> floods (2023).</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Core idea",
   "h": "Why each hazard strikes",
   "b": "<p><b>Floods</b>: heavy monsoon rain, silt-choked rivers (Kosi, the \"sorrow of Bihar\"), poor drainage, encroachment. <b>Cyclones</b>: warm Bay of Bengal and Arabian Sea, shallow coastal shelf. <b>Drought</b>: monsoon failure, rain-shadow areas (Marathwada, Rayalaseema, Bundelkhand). <b>Landslides</b>: steep young slopes, heavy rain, road cutting and tunnelling. <b>Heat waves</b>: dry north-west winds and clear skies in April-June. <b>Cloudbursts</b>: rain above 10 cm in an hour over a small area in the hills.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Debate",
   "h": "Are disasters really \"natural\"?",
   "b": "<p>Scholars argue that disasters are <b>social</b>: the same quake kills thousands in a poor country and few in a rich one. Kerala 2018 and Chennai 2015 followed unplanned building on wetlands and bad dam management. Others stress that climate change is increasing the hazards themselves. Both views matter: reduce exposure and vulnerability, and cut emissions.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Indian angle",
   "h": "Changing risk profile",
   "b": "<p>Cities are the new frontier: urban floods in Mumbai, Chennai, Bengaluru, Hyderabad and Delhi. <b>Heat waves</b> (2024 saw record temperatures in north India) and <b>lightning</b> kill many each year. Himalayan states face glacial floods and landslides. India has the <b>Vulnerability Atlas</b> (BMTPC) for housing and a national flood and landslide mapping effort.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Exam lens",
   "cls": "exam",
   "h": "How to write this",
   "b": "<div class=\"box\"><h4>Likely questions</h4><p>\"Discuss the vulnerability profile of India to natural hazards.\" (15 marks)</p><p>\"Why are urban floods increasing in India? Suggest measures.\" (10 marks)</p></div><p><b>Structure:</b> define; classify; numbers; causes (natural plus human); recent cases; link to the framework in the next lesson.</p><p><b>Prelims tip:</b> DM Act 2005; Sendai Framework (2015-2030); Bhopal 1984 is the worst industrial disaster; Kerala floods 2018.</p>"
  }
 ],
